+		False means that lower transport no longer owns this transaction.
+		Application delivery is established by the receiving application.
+
+	boolean CancelSend(uint64 transfer)
+
+		Package extension with the same owner authorization as Send.
+		Cancels the exact outstanding transaction returned by SendUnqueued,
+		including its timers and pending bearer repetitions. Returns true
+		when a transaction was cancelled, or false when it already ended.
+		Repeated cancellation is safe. The next queued transaction for
+		the destination can then start. Use identifiers only with the
+		node identity that issued them.
